OK, here is a report on where we currently stand so far, on a decision
of whether or not to have a jbonunsla 2007 at Penguicon. There are
currently only two people, Robin Lee Powell and Matt Dunlap, who would
probably attend. Everyone is happy to see a Lojban Festival happen at
Penguicon 2007, but five of you (komfo,amonan, jcowan, lojbab, kamsen,
bancus) sent their regrets.

I don't wish to run another jbonunsla at Philcon, and I would need at
least a half-dozen out-of-state attendees to justify setting aside
space at Penguicon and do all that labor. Unless I get them within the
next month or so, there won't be a jbonunsla in 2007. This is not
necessarily a bad thing. We could declare it an every-two-years event,
and it might increase demand for one in 2008.

-Eppcott


